Generated clients: text derived from Apache-2.0 inputs
------------------------------------------------------

The files under `src/*/generated/*/` are written by the generators of
tools/build/proto-codegen (see docs/design/generated_sources.md). Each file's
first lines name its generator and the sha256 of every input. The inputs
themselves are not committed here; the archives are pinned by sha256 and
fetched at build time.

1. AWS clients (`komira_aws_*`). Generated from the AWS service models
   (`service-2.json`) and endpoint rulesets of botocore, pinned in
   third_party/botocore/BUCK (version and archive sha256 there). botocore is
   licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and its NOTICE reads:

       Botocore
       Copyright 2012-2022 Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.

   (The rest of botocore's NOTICE concerns the vendored parts of the
   `requests` library inside botocore's Python code; none of that is read or
   reproduced here.) botocore's LICENSE.txt and NOTICE are extracted
   unmodified from the archive as `//third_party/botocore:files[LICENSE.txt]`
   and `[NOTICE]`.

2. Google Cloud clients (`komira_gcp_*`) and other code generated from the
   googleapis `.proto` files. Generated from the files of
   https://github.com/googleapis/googleapis (Apache License, Version 2.0; it
   ships no NOTICE), at the commit pinned in tools/vendor/googleapis/BUCK.
   The archive's LICENSE is extracted unmodified as
   `//tools/vendor/googleapis:googleapis[LICENSE]`. Each googleapis file
   carries its own license header, which
   names the owner of the definitions the generated text derives from.

The Apache License, Version 2.0 is at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
and in the LICENSE file of this repository. The generated files are modified
forms of the inputs' definitions (their structure re-expressed as Mojo); they
are distributed here under the same license as the rest of komira.
